          28,
          36,
          44,
          52,
          60
        ],
        "text": "Marcus was three minutes into his set at the basement club when Dana, from the back table, called out that she'd seen this exact routine two years ago and that even his wife had walked out during it. The room turned on him with a roar of laughter; he lost his place in his notes, tried the punchline anyway, and got nothing but Dana repeating the line back at him in his own cadence until the laughter came again, louder. He set the microphone in its stand, said thanks, and walked off with eight minutes still on the clock while she took a slow sip of her beer. Later a server stacked the chairs and turned off the string lights over the stage.",
        "suffix": "\n\nSummarize the preceding story in one sentence.",
